What is derived from it
-----------------------

Presentation only: the ink-on-paper colour system, the type and spacing rhythm,
the three motion curves, the "sketch" border-radius idiom, and the general shape
of several DOM/CSS patterns (torn-paper cards, the hand-drawn scrollbar, the
paper-tear loading transition, the sr-only/skip-link accessibility layer).

These are reimplemented here for a different application; no file is copied
verbatim. The MIT licence text is reproduced in LICENSE-portfolio-itom.

What is NOT used
----------------

The upstream README states:

    "All personal assets, 3D textures, images, and copywriting are copyright of
     Tomasz Szmajda and may not be reused or reproduced without explicit
     permission."

Accordingly this project contains none of the upstream project's images,
textures, audio, fonts-as-shipped, favicon, Open Graph artwork, or copywriting,
and none of its branding. Any paper or texture imagery used here is either
generated procedurally or independently sourced.

Fonts
-----

Where the display face "Cabin Sketch" is used it is obtained directly from
Google Fonts under the SIL Open Font License 1.1, and the OFL text is shipped
alongside the font files as that licence requires. It is referenced with a
system-font fallback so the interface is fully usable without it.
